routes.brief:
First prerequisite: Gross–Zagier formulas and arithmetic heights (GrossZagierAndArithmeticHeights). Do not re-plan GZ.0–GZ.9; this Part II treats CM values of (higher) automorphic Green functions on orthogonal Shimura varieties. Start from Li, Invent. Math. 234 (2023), 375–418 (published numbering), and the Bruinier–Ehlen–Yang, Bruinier (Crelle 2012) and Bruinier–Yang (ALM 2011) results it quotes. Coalesce with PAPER-BRUINIER-EHLEN-YANG-21 (issue #1288) when that is extracted, and import the s = σ_0+1 Borcherds–Bruinier Green functions from the candidate GSpinSpecialDivisorHeights rather than building them twice.

Final theorems:
- Theorem 1.1: individual CM values on X_0(1)². Include the case d_1d_2 a square via the F = Q result (E8).
- Theorem 1.3: differences at big CM points.
- Conjecture 1.6, recorded as a statement.
- Theorem 1.7: read n = 2, i.e. n + 2 = 2d = 4 (E7).

Carriers and intermediate results, in order:
- quadratic spaces over totally real F, Res GSpin Shimura varieties and their components, special and CM cycles, and Example 2.7;
- Hilbert modular forms with the rational structures M_κ = M_κ(Q) ⊗ C, M_F and M_F^θ;
- the Rankin–Cohen operators and 𝒟 (Lemmas 2.2–2.3, Example 2.1, including Legendre polynomials);
- Kronecker's theorem and Lemmas 2.8–2.9 and Corollary 2.11, stated with the corrected hypotheses (E1–E2);
- Lemmas 3.2–3.3 and Proposition 3.4;
- Theorem 4.1 twisted by the exceptional divisor D (E6), Proposition 4.2 and Theorem 4.3 (read θ_{P_1} − θ_{P_2}, E5);
- harmonic Whittaker forms, ξ and {·,·};
- the regularized theta lift and Borcherds products over totally real fields;
- Lemmas 4.5–4.6, Proposition 4.8 and Theorem 4.10;
- the higher Green functions Φ^r_L with the integral representation (3.14);
- BEY21 Theorems 5.5, 5.10, 7.13 and BKY12 Proposition 4.6, as imported statements until their own extractions land.

Imports, never re-planned:
- harmonic Maass forms and ξ: QSeriesPartitionsAndMockModularForms QM.3;
- the Weil representation: MetaplecticAutomorphicForms MP.4;
- theta kernels: MP.5;
- the indefinite Siegel–Weil formula: MP.6;
- Siegel's formula and Hecke Eisenstein series for definite lattices: GeometryOfNumbersAndQuadraticArithmetic GN.3;
- unimodular O-lattices: GN.2;
- Baily–Borel: ShimuraVarieties V2;
- toroidal compactifications and Koecher: ShimuraCompactifications C2, C6;
- canonical models and CM reciprocity: ShimuraVarieties V4, V6;
- CM points on X_0(N): HeegnerPointEulerSystems HE.1;
- Dolbeault and analytic vanishing: ComplexComparisonPartII C1–C2;
- blow-up ampleness: SchemeAndStackFoundations SF.0;
- Mathlib's modular forms, Gamma and hypergeometric functions.

Tests:
- X_0(1)² with (d_1, d_2) = (−3, −4), r = 2 (Gross–Kohnen–Zagier's even case) and r = 1 with d_1 fundamental;
- Lemma 2.9's counterexample F(x) = ∏_{k≥1}(1 − x/2^k), c_i = 2^i, which the hypotheses must exclude;
- F = Q(√5) with a rank-8 Z-unimodular lattice from U_F^+.
